# `quality` Standalone Wire Specification

Quality is an 8-byte sortable encoding of the offer rate `in / out`. Encoding
accepts JSON `{"out": <amount>, "in": <amount>}`, computes that inverse ratio,
and writes the returned unsigned integer in big-endian order.

| Bits | Component |
| :--- | :--- |
| 63..56 | Decimal exponent plus 100 |
| 55..0 | Mantissa |

Lower unsigned encodings sort as better qualities for the taker. The JSON key
order is an easy trap: `{"out":"2","in":"1"}` decodes as `0.5`, not `2`.
Zero `out` and arithmetic failures return the zero sentinel. The standalone
payload has no field header and decode requires exactly eight bytes.

